	SAY NAME2 "Jerrod's Mace +3"
	SAY DESC "This was the favored weapon of the priest of Tempus named Jerrod. Jerrod sacrificed his life to save the town of Easthaven from the powerful devil known as Belhifet.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– The wearer and any allies within their visual radius are immune to fear and morale failure

THAC0: +3, +5 vs. demons and devils
Damage: 1d6+4, +6 vs. demons and devils
Damage type: Crushing
Speed Factor: 3
Proficiency Type: Mace
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 11 Strength

Weight: 6"





//MACE OF DISRUPTION +3 - valore 8000mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BLUN12.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Mace"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "The mace is a direct descendant of the basic club, being nothing more than a wooden shaft with a stone or iron head mounted on the end. The head design varies: Some are spiked, others flanged, and still others have pyramidal knobs.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1d6+1 (crushing)
Speed Factor: 6
Proficiency Type: Mace
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 11 Strength

Weight: 10"

	SAY NAME2 "Mace of Disruption +3"
	SAY DESC "This heavy mace was created for a very specific purpose: to slay undead. Any such creature hit by it not only feels the sting of the weapon, but also has a chance of being simply blasted from existence. There are legends that speak of a priest so holy a single glancing touch could send a vampire to oblivion, but whether the weapon empowered her or she empowered it is a topic for theologians.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Immunity to hold

Combat abilities: 
– Undead must save vs. Death at -2 or be utterly destroyed

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d6+4, +5 magical extra vs. undead
Damage type: Crushing
Speed Factor: 3
Proficiency Type: Mace
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 11 Strength

Weight: 6"





//MACE OF DISRUPTION +4 - valore 12000mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BLUN25.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Mace"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "The mace is a direct descendant of the basic club, being nothing more than a wooden shaft with a stone or iron head mounted on the end. The head design varies: Some are spiked, others flanged, and still others have pyramidal knobs.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1d6+1 (crushing)
Speed Factor: 6
Proficiency Type: Mace
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 11 Strength

Weight: 10"

	SAY NAME2 "Mace of Disruption +4"
	SAY DESC "This heavy mace was created for a very specific purpose: to slay undead. Any such creature hit by it not only feels the sting of the weapon, but also has a chance of being simply blasted from existence. There are legends that speak of a priest so holy a single glancing touch could send a vampire to oblivion, but whether the weapon empowered her or she empowered it is a topic for theologians.

Now that the mace has been coated with illithium, it is even more potent, conferring to its user immunity to the life-draining powers of the more powerful undead.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Immunity to Hold
– Immunity to Level Drain

Combat abilities:
– Undead must save vs. Death at -4 or be utterly destroyed

THAC0: +4
Damage: 1d6+5, +10 magical damage extra vs. undead
Damage type: Crushing
Speed Factor: 2
Proficiency Type: Mace
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 11 Strength

Weight: 6"



//ROD OF ATROPHY +5 - valore 10000mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/RODS02.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Rod"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Rods are about three feet long and as thick as your thumb. They are normally found in cases or similar storage places. Rods can be fashioned from metal, wood, ivory, or bone. They can be plain or decorated and carved, tipped, or not. Rods are powered by charges, unless noted otherwise in the description of a particular rod. Each time the rod is used, one or more charge may be expended.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 3"

	SAY NAME2 "Rod of Atrophy +5"
	SAY DESC "This mace, forged from a strange, translucent alloy that seems to hum with an unsettling vibration, was never intended for traditional warfare. Legends say it was crafted by a cabal of wizard-smiths who sought a weapon that could strike the spirit rather than the flesh. The head of the mace does not truly hit its target in the physical sense; instead, it passes through armor and bone like a ghostly mist, discharging a surge of pure arcane energy directly into the victim's life force. While it leaves no bruises or broken bones, those struck by the Ethereal Lash feel their very essence beginning to unravel, leaving them fragile and drained as the weapon systematically deconstructs their magical and physical defenses.

STATISTICS:

Combat abilities:
- On hit target suffers Ray of Enfeeblement

THAC0: +5
Damage: 10d4 (save vs. Wand for half), no Strength bonus
Damage type: Magical
Speed Factor: 0
Proficiency Type: Mace
Type: One-handed
Range: 1 yard
Requires:
 3 Strength

Weight: 1"





//STORM STAR +4 - valore 8000mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BLUN28.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Mace"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "The mace is a direct descendant of the basic club, being nothing more than a wooden shaft with a stone or iron head mounted on the end. The head design varies: Some are spiked, others flanged, and still others have pyramidal knobs.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1d6+1 (crushing)
Speed Factor: 6
Proficiency Type: Mace
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 11 Strength

Weight: 10"

	SAY NAME2 "Storm Star +4"
	SAY DESC "The Storm Star is a weapon born of the tempest, forged in a place where the Elemental Plane of Air bleeds into the Material Plane. Legend has it that the first of these maces was gifted by Akadi, Queen of the Air, to a mortal champion who defended her shrines. The head of the mace is crafted from a strange, silver-blue alloy that crackles with spectacular arcs of lightning when wielded.

STATISTICS:

THAC0: +4
Damage: 1d6+5, +2 electricity damage
Damage type: Crushing
Speed Factor: 2
Proficiency Type: Mace
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 11 Strength

Weight: 5"






